yrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I had a more in-depth look at the order in which things were happening, I somewhat understand why scripts are being loaded out of order, I will try to make a proper MRP and update #105926 accordingly.\r\n\r\nThe root issue is actually cyclic dependency where we want to load class A, which checks for some values in class B, which itself holds references to class A and children of class A, so now we're also trying to load those child classes, which obviously depend on class A, and at that point it looks like the child classes have their docs generated, or at least some of them (and they get the `RefCounted` treatment), then class A gets its docs generated, and the remaining children of class A get properly documented.","created_at":"2025-05-11T07:29:38Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T07:29:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#discussion_r2083436791","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2083436791"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#discussion_r2083436791"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2083436791/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":344,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2083389510,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"po